<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-06T13:52:30+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Sun, 06 Sep 2026 13:52:30 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[A 2021 landslide cut Denali’s only road; five years later, a $230M bridge spans the slope]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133797517.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A new bridge now spans the Denali National Park road after a landslide. This $230 million project reconnects the eastern and western road sections. Engineers built a 475-foot steel truss bridge over the unstable moving ground. Hikers and cyclists can now cross the bridge, while bus service resumes in 2027. This marks a long-term solution for accessing remote park areas.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2021-a-landslide-cut-denali-national-parks-only-road-in-two-five-years-later-a-230-million-475-foot-bridge-has-been-built-directly-above-the-still-moving-slope/articleshow/133797517.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2021-a-landslide-cut-denali-national-parks-only-road-in-two-five-years-later-a-230-million-475-foot-bridge-has-been-built-directly-above-the-still-moving-slope/articleshow/133797517.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T13:02:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133797923,imgsize-1888285.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colorado ranch listed for $5.9M as development site, bought by conservationists instead]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133827621.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A 674-acre ranch on Colorado’s Pikes Peak was listed for $5.9 million as a potential development site, but Palmer Land Conservancy bought it for conservation instead. The Pinestone Ranch property connects Woodland Park with more than 100,000 acres of public land and could eventually support trails, wildlife habitat and public access as part of wider efforts to complete the Ring the Peak route.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-674-acre-colorado-ranch-was-listed-for-5-9-million-as-a-development-site-conservationists-bought-it-instead-permanently-protecting-land-that-links-to-more-than-100000-acres-of-public-space/articleshow/133827621.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-674-acre-colorado-ranch-was-listed-for-5-9-million-as-a-development-site-conservationists-bought-it-instead-permanently-protecting-land-that-links-to-more-than-100000-acres-of-public-space/articleshow/133827621.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133829671,imgsize-212257.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How discarded Christmas trees are being used to build dunes on a UK beach]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133826930.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Discarded Christmas trees are being used to strengthen the sand dunes at St Annes beach on England’s Fylde Coast. Since the project began in 2013, the trees have helped trap wind-blown sand and expand the dunes. The wider dunes act as a natural sea defence, helping protect nearby homes and businesses from coastal flooding while also creating habitat for specialised plants and wildlife.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2013-a-uk-beach-began-planting-discarded-christmas-trees-to-trap-blowing-sand-by-2026-the-project-had-created-90-metres-of-new-dunes-that-help-defend-homes-from-flooding/articleshow/133826930.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-2013-a-uk-beach-began-planting-discarded-christmas-trees-to-trap-blowing-sand-by-2026-the-project-had-created-90-metres-of-new-dunes-that-help-defend-homes-from-flooding/articleshow/133826930.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T11:58:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133827477,imgsize-116629.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Four private Michigan islands spanning 520 acres hit the market for $2.3 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133772820.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Now on the market for $2.3 million, this exclusive private group of four islands spans 520 acres. It features a beautifully renovated home, essential machinery, two boats, and a dock slip on the mainland. With about 2,000 feet of waterfront along Michigan's northern border, most of the property is safeguarded by a conservation easement, preserving the area’s native ecosystems and ensuring enjoyment for generations to come.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/four-private-michigan-islands-spanning-520-acres-hit-the-market-for-2-3-million-the-deal-includes-a-home-two-boats-and-land-protected-by-a-conservation-easement/articleshow/133772820.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/four-private-michigan-islands-spanning-520-acres-hit-the-market-for-2-3-million-the-deal-includes-a-home-two-boats-and-land-protected-by-a-conservation-easement/articleshow/133772820.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T11:58:47+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133773129,imgsize-1054520.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Both pilots killed as Greek fighter jet crashes during air show near Athens]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133827381.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/both-pilots-killed-as-greek-fighter-jet-crashes-during-air-show-near-athens/articleshow/133827381.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/both-pilots-killed-as-greek-fighter-jet-crashes-during-air-show-near-athens/articleshow/133827381.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T11:39:58+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133828002,imgsize-35877.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[TikTok Dog Dies At 8: Internet star Tucker Budzyn dies after chemo complication; fans mourn online]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133818879.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Tucker Budzyn, the beloved golden retriever who became a TikTok and social media sensation, has died at eight after a sudden complication during lymphoma treatment. His owner, Courtney Budzyn, said Tucker initially responded well to chemotherapy and entered partial remission before an intestinal infection rapidly worsened his condition. Despite emergency treatment, veterinarians could not save him. Courtney shared an emotional tribute, saying Tucker was “part of my soul,” as fans mourned his loss.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/we-had-to-let-him-go-tiktok-famous-golden-retriever-tucker-budzyn-dies-at-8-after-sudden-complications-from-lymphoma/articleshow/133818879.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/we-had-to-let-him-go-tiktok-famous-golden-retriever-tucker-budzyn-dies-at-8-after-sudden-complications-from-lymphoma/articleshow/133818879.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T05:32:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133818932,imgsize-81718.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Akademiks Mocks Travis Scott: DJ blasts rapper after Yeat’s ‘ON NOTHING’ diss; feud motive remains unclear]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133819117.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[YouTuber DJ Akademiks has weighed in on Yeat’s fiery diss aimed at Travis Scott in “ON NOTHING.” Akademiks questioned why Yeat targeted Travis instead of Playboi Carti and mocked the Houston rapper over what he called a string of recent losses. The diss followed Yeat’s removed verse from Young Thug’s “Eaters,” sparking fan speculation about tension between the rappers. Neither Travis nor Yeat has confirmed what triggered the clash.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/i-aint-got-no-respect-for-you-youtuber-dj-akademiks-mocks-travis-scott-after-yeats-explosive-diss-track-takes-aim-at-the-rapper/articleshow/133819117.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/i-aint-got-no-respect-for-you-youtuber-dj-akademiks-mocks-travis-scott-after-yeats-explosive-diss-track-takes-aim-at-the-rapper/articleshow/133819117.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T05:52:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Global Sports Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133819186,imgsize-90519.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists exposed a Wisconsin forest to extra CO₂ for 11 years; productivity rose 39%, but ozone cut gains]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133796967.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Wisconsin experiment studied forest communities exposed to high carbon dioxide and ozone. Elevated carbon dioxide significantly increased forest productivity and carbon storage over eleven years. Conversely, increased ozone levels reduced forest productivity and ecosystem carbon content. The combined effects showed carbon dioxide stimulating growth and ozone limiting it. These findings highlight forests' complex responses to atmospheric changes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-altered-the-air-around-a-wisconsin-forest-for-11-years-extra-co2-drove-39-more-productivity-but-ozone-reversed-part-of-the-gain/articleshow/133796967.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-altered-the-air-around-a-wisconsin-forest-for-11-years-extra-co2-drove-39-more-productivity-but-ozone-reversed-part-of-the-gain/articleshow/133796967.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T10:36:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133797442,imgsize-2299318.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[147 years after Hall Effect discovery, scientists find it works in-plane]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133826353.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1879-edwin-hall-discovered-an-electrical-effect-thought-to-need-a-perpendicular-magnetic-field-147-years-later-scientists-have-shown-it-can-work-with-the-field-in-plane/articleshow/133826353.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1879-edwin-hall-discovered-an-electrical-effect-thought-to-need-a-perpendicular-magnetic-field-147-years-later-scientists-have-shown-it-can-work-with-the-field-in-plane/articleshow/133826353.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-06T10:36:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133826449,imgsize-781465.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Utah's rocky slopes hide nearly 1 billion tons of water, gravity study reveals]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133817725.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/scientists-discover-nearly-1-billion-tons-of-water-locked-inside-utahs-rocky-glaciers-using-gravity-measurements-to-map-ice-buried-beneath-mountain-debris/articleshow/133817725.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[h